WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.940
The Star Wars films are starting to dig a
little deeper into the backstories of its

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.799
most popular characters, starting with a Han
Solo prequel that features Alden Ehrenreich

00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:12.650
in the role originally played by Harrison
Ford.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.690
If that film is successful enough, it'll likely
increase interest in peeks at some of the

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:21.090
other characters' pasts — and who has a
more interesting history than Princess Leia

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.090
Organa?

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.410
Sure, we got to see how her parents got together
during the Star Wars prequel trilogy, but

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.870
there are a lot of dots still to connect.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.510
Like, who taught her the secret Jedi art of
space-insults?

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.540
"I don't know where you get your delusions,
laser brain."

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.680
The late, great Carrie Fisher unquestionably
made the role her own, and left some big boots

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.360
to fill with her untimely passing in December
2016.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.790
Re-casting Leia would be about more than just
tracking down a doppelgänger for Fisher.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.540
The actress would have to have some wit, sass,
and class to offer, too.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.000
Here are a few young actresses who might just
be equipped to pick up the old blaster and

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.100
bring Leia back to life.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.719
Millie Bobby Brown

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:05.740
Stranger Things starlet Millie Bobby Brown
has already put her hat into the ring by declaring

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:09.520
that she'd love to play a young Princess Leia
in a prequel.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.650
Thanks to her breakout role as Eleven in Netflix's
sci-fi sensation, Brown has already proven

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.340
she can hold her own in an on-screen fight.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.659
And her time on shows like ABC's Once Upon
a Time had her grappling with the sort of

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:26.450
high fantasy and science fiction world that
any young Leia would encounter in a new Star

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.689
Wars movie.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.909
That means she's used to tackling tough scripts
filled with weird character names and alien

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:33.409
species from around the galaxy.

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:35.569
"I couldn't say 'demogorgon' at first.

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:37.849
It was like, 'dum dum duhhh.'"

00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:42.500
Even better, Brown's got the same brown eyes
and hair as Leia, along with similar facial

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.829
bone structure, so it's easy to picture her
adopting the role without a hitch.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:48.389
Rowan Blanchard

00:01:48.389 --> 00:01:53.049
Another young actress who looks like a ringer
for young Leia is Girl Meets World star Rowan

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:54.270
Blanchard.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.939
Like Brown, Blanchard has already had her
fair share of high-action moments on screen,

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:03.780
thanks to her turn in Spy Kids 4 — and she's
also one to watch right now, as she'll star

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.860
in Ava Duvernay's live-action adaptation of
A Wrinkle in Time, giving her fantasy cred

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.560
as well as a major platform from which to
launch her film career.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.230
"The world has presented me with an opportunity."

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:19.840
Perhaps most importantly, Blanchard also seems
to have a youthful sense of wisdom and wit

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.830
that would be an absolute necessity for playing
young Leia.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.570
Mackenzie Foy

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:30.250
She might be best known for her work as a
half-vampire love child in The Twilight Saga's

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.970
final film, but Mackenzie Foy has also proven
herself a capable young talent on the rise:

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.060
she shared the screen with Matthew McConaughey
in Christopher Nolan's Interstellar and she

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:45.540
has a lead role in Lasse Hallström's upcoming
take on The Nutcracker and the Four Realms.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.420
In much the way the young Carrie Fisher carried
herself with a sense of self-confidence and

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:54.330
capability mixed with softness, Foy has the
same kind of steady composure that could suit

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.840
a new take on the Princess.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.460
Kiernan Shipka

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:03.939
Throughout Mad Men's six seasons, Kiernan
Shipka grew into the secret MVP of the series,

00:03:03.939 --> 00:03:07.010
especially where its youngest cast members
were concerned.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:11.850
While the actors playing her brother Bobby
came and went without much fuss, Shipka blossomed

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:16.560
into an important presence on the show as
Sally, sturdily running counter to her parents'

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.070
selfish behavior before subtly adopting some
of their traits.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:24.030
Shipka can not only deliver a sharp-tongued
line like nobody's business …

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.819
"You think you could take me."

00:03:25.819 --> 00:03:26.819
"Heh.

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:27.819
I think I could."

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:28.819
"Well, you're wrong."

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.790
...but she's also able to impart nuance and
curiosity to situations to enrich a scene

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.770
that might otherwise fall flat.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:40.100
A Princess Leia backstory would need those
traits in abundance, so she might just be

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.040
a good match for the movie.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.569
Sophia Lillis

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:48.030
She might not be a household name just yet,
but Sophia Lillis is also well on her way

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.630
to becoming an important young actress.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:55.430
She not only possesses the same kind of stoicism
that helped define Leia onscreen, but she's

00:03:55.430 --> 00:04:00.709
also starring in the new film adaptation of
Stephen King's It as the unconquerable Beverly

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:01.709
Marsh.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:04.709
That means she'll start to be on the star
track sooner than later.

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:09.630
She's also another close visual ringer for
young Carrie Fisher — a pair of brown contacts

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:14.290
and those signature cinnamon bun locks are
all it'd take to make the transformation complete.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:19.191
Of course, as good as any of those options
could be, there's really only one young actress

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:22.889
who could truly do the role the justice it
deserves...

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:23.889
Billie Lourd

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:28.169
The fact that Billie Lourd is Fisher's own
daughter means she certainly deserves more

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:30.050
than a little consideration.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.379
From what we've seen of her screen appearances
in Scream Queens and other roles, she also

00:04:34.379 --> 00:04:38.490
seems to have inherited Fisher's signature
tenacity and deep sense of humor.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:43.360
Lourd made a cameo appearance in Star Wars:
The Force Awakens and told reporters, "I wish

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.129
I played a young princess."

00:04:45.129 --> 00:04:47.949
Who better to manage her mother's legacy than
Lourd?

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:49.259
Plus, let's face it.

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:51.139
She's Leia's closest look-alike.

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:53.300
It's actually kinda spooky how similar they
are.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:59.569
"I try to do my own thing, but when I'm wearing
something like *this* it's kind of hard to

00:04:59.569 --> 00:05:02.009
escape the comparison."

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:03.009
Thanks for watching!

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:05.490
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.409
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

